      <MissionDesc>Children of The Immaculate Heart Exists to promote the dignity of the human person and to uphold the goodness and beauty of both the masculine and feminine genius. Specifically, Children of The Immaculate Heart serves men, women, and children who are vulnerable due to human trafficking, the commercial sexual exploitation of children, pornography, and the contraceptive and abortion industries. Because human trafficking relies upon the pornography, contraceptive, and abortion industries, CIH seeks to evangelize both the individual human heart and society as a whole so that the aforementioned evils might no longer be causing damage to individuals and our country as a whole. Outreach work will be done to meet women and children in the places where they are at risk. Children of The Immaculate Heart will provide after care for those who want to get out of prostitution, trafficking, or other forms of sexual exploitation. Such care includes the education, job training, physical, psychological,</MissionDesc>
      <SignificantNewProgramSrvcInd>false</SignificantNewProgramSrvcInd>
      <SignificantChangeInd>false</SignificantChangeInd>
      <ExpenseAmt>245822</ExpenseAmt>
      <Desc>In 2024, the St. Bakhita's Program provided specialized support to 29 women who are survivors of sex trafficking. We focus on helping those who have children, as they often face greater challenges in finding housing and accessing other services. We also serve single women. Our core services include:-Case management-Housing navigation and rental assistance-Individual and family counseling-Financial coachingWe also connect clients with other community providers for any additional support they may need. Our program offers an intensive level of care, with our case manager and counselor available to meet with each woman weekly. We assist with both their material needs and provide the human and spiritual support necessary for their journey to recovery.</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>182637</ExpenseAmt>
        <Desc>Children of the Immaculate Heart began offering emergency services in the fall of 2023, and the first full year of these services was in 2024. We launched a mobile clinic that enables us to respond to survivors of sex trafficking within 24 hours of them contacting us. Our Program Administrator meets with the individual seeking help at a safe, neutral location like a coffee shop or park to conduct a needs assessment. From there, we help her find safe housing. Once she is secure, we connect her with a case manager from St. Bakhita's Program for longer-term support. In 2024, we provided emergency services to over 29 women.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
